module lamd-local-rules.local-rules

import core.frcp6.{ frcp6 }

// The Middle District of Louisiana's own civil periods, computed under the
// federal rules (FRCP 6(a) governs "any local rule"). Reply memoranda may
// be filed without leave only on Rule 12 and Rule 56 motions; a reply on
// any other motion, and any surreply, needs leave (LR 7(f)). The court may
// shorten or lengthen the response period for good cause (LR 7(f)). LR
// 7(a) allows one ex parte extension of time to plead of twenty-one days
// from the time the pleading would otherwise be due, on the movant's
// certification of no previous extension and no objection of record; it
// extends an FRCP period and declares none of its own, so it stays in this
// note. Objections to an item of costs "within fourteen days" (LR 54(d))
// state no starting event, so they stay in this note; review of the
// clerk's taxation within seven days (LR 54(e)) is FRCP 54(d)(1)'s period
// and belongs to lit/frcp. The court's own grounds for dismissal for lack
// of prosecution (no service within 90 days of filing, no responsive
// pleading or default within sixty days of service, six months without
// proceedings: LR 41(b)(1)) and for a returned address left uncorrected
// for thirty days (LR 41(b)(4)) are court actions, so they stay in this
// note. The hospital-records production window (no earlier than ten
// working days before trial: LR 45) and attorney discipline (LR 83) are
// not encoded. Rules that state no period or limit stay out: memoranda
// (7(d)), motions needing no memorandum (7(e)), the motion in limine
// conference (7(h)), the privilege log (26(c)) and review of a magistrate
// judge's order (72(a)). The earlier M.D. La. outline's FRCP flow and its
// decisions (Twombly, Iqbal, Celotex, Anderson, Matsushita, Frow v. De La
// Vega) are FRCP authority and belong to lit/frcp; they are removed here:
// no reporter text is vendored.
/// A memorandum, including a brief, a memorandum supporting or opposing a
/// motion and an appeal to a District Judge: at most twenty-five pages
/// excluding attachments, tables and the certificate of service, unless
/// leave is obtained (M.D. La. LR 7(g)).
limit memorandum { pages <= 25 cite "M.D. La. LR 7(g)" } cite "M.D. La. LR 7(g)"
/// A reply or surreply memorandum, if permitted: at most ten pages
/// (M.D. La. LR 7(g)).
limit reply-memorandum { pages <= 10 cite "M.D. La. LR 7(g)" } cite "M.D. La. LR 7(g)"

/// A motion is served (M.D. La. LR 7(f)).
event MotionServed() paper memorandum
/// A response to a motion is served (M.D. La. LR 7(f)).
event ResponseServed() paper memorandum
/// A reply memorandum on a Rule 12 or Rule 56 motion is filed
/// (M.D. La. LR 7(f)).
event ReplyFiled() paper reply-memorandum
/// The scheduling conference (M.D. La. LR 26(a)).
event SchedulingConference()
/// The Case Management Conference (M.D. La. LR 26(b)).
event CaseManagementConference()
/// The discovery deadline of the scheduling order passes
/// (M.D. La. LR 26(d)).
event DiscoveryDeadline()
/// Notice of a proposed dismissal for failure to prosecute is mailed to
/// the plaintiff (M.D. La. LR 41(b)).
event ProsecutionNoticeMailed()
/// An order dismissing the action for failure to prosecute is entered
/// (M.D. La. LR 41(b)).
event ProsecutionDismissalOrdered()
/// The party in whose favor judgment is rendered receives notice of entry
/// of judgment (M.D. La. LR 54(c)).
event JudgmentEntryNoticed()
/// The clerk enters default (M.D. La. LR 55).
event DefaultEntered()
/// A reply statement of material facts that asks that a statement be
/// stricken is served (M.D. La. LR 56(e)).
event ReplyStatementServed()
/// The case is finally disposed of (M.D. La. LR 79(f)).
event FinalDisposition()

/// M.D. La. LR 7(f): each respondent opposing a motion files a response,
/// with opposing affidavits and supporting documents then available,
/// within twenty-one days after service of the motion.
deadline response-period: 21.days after MotionServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. La. LR 7(f)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// M.D. La. LR 7(f): a reply memorandum on a Rule 12 or Rule 56 motion is
/// filed within fourteen days after service of the response.
deadline reply-period: 14.days after ResponseServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. La. LR 7(f)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// M.D. La. LR 26(a)(3): any meeting of the parties is held in time for
/// its report to be filed no later than two weeks prior to the date of the
/// scheduling conference.
deadline rule26f-report-period: 2.weeks before SchedulingConference() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. La. LR 26(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// M.D. La. LR 26(b): initial disclosures under FRCP 26(a)(1) are made no
/// later than seven days before the Case Management Conference, unless a
/// court order sets a different time or a party objects at the attorney
/// conference.
deadline initial-disclosure-period: 7.days before CaseManagementConference() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. La. LR 26(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// M.D. La. LR 26(d)(1): absent exceptional circumstances, a discovery
/// motion filed after the discovery deadline is timely only if filed
/// within seven days after the deadline and it concerns conduct in the
/// final seven days of discovery.
deadline late-discovery-motion-period: 7.days after DiscoveryDeadline() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. La. LR 26(d)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// M.D. La. LR 41(b)(2): before a dismissal for failure to prosecute, the
/// plaintiff has fourteen calendar days from mailing of the notice to file
/// evidence of good cause; with no response in time the court may dismiss.
deadline prosecution-good-cause-period: 14.days after ProsecutionNoticeMailed() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. La. LR 41(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// M.D. La. LR 41(b)(3): a dismissal for failure to prosecute is without
/// prejudice, and the order allows reinstatement within thirty days for
/// good cause shown.
deadline reinstatement-period: 30.days after ProsecutionDismissalOrdered() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. La. LR 41(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// M.D. La. LR 54(c): within thirty days after receiving notice of entry
/// of judgment, unless otherwise ordered, the party allowed costs serves
/// and files a notice of application to tax costs with a supporting
/// memorandum.
deadline costs-application-period: 30.days after JudgmentEntryNoticed() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. La. LR 54(c)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// M.D. La. LR 55: a judgment of default is not entered until fourteen
/// days after entry of default; this is the earliest date, not a last
/// day.
deadline default-judgment-waiting-period: 14.days after DefaultEntered() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. La. LR 55"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// M.D. La. LR 56(e): a request to strike made in a reply statement of
/// material facts may be answered by a response filed within 14 days of
/// service of the reply statement.
deadline strike-request-response-period: 14.days after ReplyStatementServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. La. LR 56(e)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// M.D. La. LR 79(f): exhibits in the clerk's custody are removed within
/// thirty days of the final disposition of the case, or may be destroyed
/// or otherwise disposed of by the clerk.
deadline exhibit-removal-period: 30.days after FinalDisposition() counted_by frcp6 cite "M.D. La. LR 79(f)"
{
  forum frcp
}
